WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.688
Compliance usually arrives as
a package assembled at the end.

2
00:00:03.688 --> 00:00:06.501
Modernization is the one
moment that can change,

3
00:00:06.501 --> 00:00:10.088
because you're choosing the
platform and the pipeline anyway.

4
00:00:10.088 --> 00:00:14.806
A control the platform carries once is
inherited by every application on it, and

5
00:00:14.806 --> 00:00:19.738
a pipeline that keeps its results produces
evidence without anyone collecting it.

6
00:00:19.738 --> 00:00:20.901
Two more points.

7
00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:24.975
Legacy is itself a compliance
matter: an application kept on

8
00:00:24.975 --> 00:00:29.212
unsupported software needs a plan,
a risk acceptance and a date.

9
00:00:29.212 --> 00:00:33.258
And privacy and records officials
come in at design review,

10
00:00:33.258 --> 00:00:37.387
when a new data store, a new flow
or an AI feature first appears.

11
00:00:37.387 --> 00:00:39.120
So who makes all these calls?
